---
import { mcpTools } from '../../data/jetbrains-plugin'
---

<section class="section" id="ai-agents">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">AI agents</span>
      <h2>Ask your agent, the plugin answers</h2>
      <p>
        The plugin adds ten tools to the MCP server bundled with JetBrains IDEs. Your agent gets facts the plugin already worked
        out: topics behind Spring properties, payload types, consumer groups, what a broker holds right now.
      </p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Enable the server in <em>Settings → Tools → MCP Server</em> and copy its configuration into your agent.</li>
        <li>Run <em>Tools → Install AsyncAPI Agent Skill</em>. It writes <code>.claude/skills/asyncapi/SKILL.md</code>, which tells the agent which tool answers which question.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="note">
        Finding and validating documents is free. <code>asyncapi_connections</code> and <code>asyncapi_topology</code> are the same tools{' '}
        <a href="https://kurkik.pavelon.dev">Kurkik</a> serves with <code>kurkik mcp</code> in a terminal.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Ask your agent</th><th scope="col">Tool</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            mcpTools.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <td>“{t.ask}”</td>
                <td><code>{t.tool}</code></td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.3rem);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .steps {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .table {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  th {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  td code {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
